module default_named.neg_1

// ONE seeded cause: a parameter with a DEFAULT is passed POSITIONALLY.
//
// D102 makes a defaulted parameter keyword-only, and the reason is the rule's
// whole purpose: `connect("h", false, true)` is unreadable, so the language
// turns a style remark into a compile error. For an AI-first language that
// converts a class of generated bugs into a refusal.
//
// AGREEMENT, and it was measured before this file existed (2026-08-23): the
// oracle refuses the same shape, naming the same parameter and the same rule
// (its wording is Russian; the outcome is what a fixture pair asserts). So this
// pins a RULE of the language, not a divergence.
fn bump(x int, by int = 2) -> int => x + by

fn main() {
    println(bump(5, 2))
}
